00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:14.330
gradients. What that means is that when you're training a very deep network, your derivatives or your slopes can sometimes get either very, very big or

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:20.150
very, very small, maybe even exponentially small, and this makes training difficult. In this video,

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:26.570
you see what this problem of exploding or that vanishing gradients really means as well as how you can use

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:32.490
careful choices of the random weight initialization to significantly reduce this problem.

